Lee is a 2023 British biographical war drama film directed by Ellen Kuras in her feature directorial debut, from a screenplay by Liz Hannah, John Collee
and Marion Hume, and story from Hume, Collee and Lem Dobbs, adapted from the 1985 biography The Lives of Lee Miller by Antony Penrose.

11
00:58:29,999 --> 00:58:35,999
It stars Kate Winslet as WWII journalist Lee Miller.

12
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
The cast includes Marion Cotillard, Andrea Riseborough, Andy Samberg, Noémie
Merlant, Josh O'Connor and Alexander Skarsgård in supporting roles.

13
01:09:08,181 --> 01:09:14,181
The movie took eight years to make and, at one point, due to precarious funding, Winslet (who
also produced the movie) paid the entire cast and crew's salaries for two weeks.

14
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
The film made its world premiere at the Toronto
International Film Festival on 9 September 2023.

15
01:19:46,363 --> 01:19:52,363
It was released theatrically in the United Kingdom
by Sky Cinema on 13 September 2024.

16
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
Lee received generally positive reviews from critics and
became Sky UK's highest-grossing original film.

17
01:30:24,545 --> 01:30:30,545
It grossed $24.6 million worldwide.

18
01:35:43,636 --> 01:35:49,636
For her performance in the film, Winslet received nominations for Best
Actress at the Golden Globe Awards and AACTA International Awards.

19
01:41:02,727 --> 01:41:08,727
Additionally, the film received a nomination from
BAFTA for Outstanding British Film.

20
01:46:21,818 --> 01:46:27,818
The film explores themes of nazi, photographer,
photography, concentration camp, holocaust (shoah).

21
